      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BUDINO (3) gets the nod on the strength of two runs that are better than the raw finishing positions suggest. She was only beaten just over three lengths at this track last start despite interference in the home straight, and her Belmont Park fifth behind Treasured Legacy had merit after starting big odds and finishing within two lengths. Looks the one to beat. VIVALDA (2) gets the blinkers on for the first time today after getting back and finishing strongly over 1100m. Can sit a touch closer this time and she can put her best foot forward. FILLING WITH WATER (5) was well held first-up when beaten six lengths after leading, but she is lightly raced and the apprentice claim gives her a chance to sharpen second-up. CARBARLOTT (4) drops out of a BM44+ after a sound York debut, with weight relief and natural improvement making her the value danger if she handles the quick back-up. HARD TO TOP (1) is next best.",
